WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.020
Space is unbelievably strange.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.940
You would be forgiven for thinking that every
planet out there is similar, just a big ball

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.090
of rock and gas, but planets are remarkably
more unique than that.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:20.850
Here's the top 10 strangest planets in the
known universe, that seem like they belong

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:31.080
in some bizarre science fiction series.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:37.609
First up is this dark, menacing planet affectionately
named TrES-2b.

00:00:37.609 --> 00:00:43.679
It is located 750 light years away from our
solar system.

00:00:43.679 --> 00:00:49.319
As far as we know it is officially the darkest
planet in the entire universe.

00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:56.059
It reflects less than 1% of all light that
hits it, making it significantly darker than

00:00:56.059 --> 00:00:58.539
the majority of known exoplanets.

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:05.170
It's ominously dark surface can be partially
explained by the light absorbent gasses that

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.670
make up the bulk of the planet.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:13.050
But scientists don't really know for sure
why it is so dark.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:19.640
But it gets creepier, not only does this evil
looking ball of gas not reflect any light,

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:27.329
it actually glows a molten red colour, as
if it's a hot ball of coal on a fire.

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:36.259
The surface of the planet is a punishing 1,100
degrees Celsius, which is so hot that it glows

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:38.009
red.

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:41.119
This next planet is anything but dark.

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:46.770
In fact it sparkles luminescently in space,
just like a diamond.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:52.070
Because, well, it is in fact a gigantic diamond.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:58.440
Yes that's right this planet named 55 Cancri
e is about twice the size of earth and a third

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.469
of it is made up of solid diamond.

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:07.700
The planet is very carbon heavy, and the planet
is so dense that all carbon is in the form

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.869
of solid diamond.

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:16.330
But don't get too excited, the diamond planet
is located a spectacular 40 light years away

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.330
from Earth.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:22.090
And even if you could travel that far and
retrieve the endless supply of diamonds it

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.470
has to offer.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:28.720
There is so much diamond on the planet that
bringing even a minute fraction of it back

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:35.310
to Earth, would completely overwhelm the diamond
supply and therefore make diamonds completely

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.650
worthless.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:41.640
So this beautiful planet is best admired from
afar.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:48.090
This next planet seems to defy everything
you thought you knew about chemistry, because

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.100
it's a giant ball of ice, on fire.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.810
Imagine for a second you're on the ice planet
Hoth from Star Wars.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:03.560
That's exactly what Gliese 436 b would look
like except that the icy surface is constantly

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.830
burning at 439 degrees Celsius.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.970
So how can this be?

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:17.830
How can ice defy the laws of chemistry and
stay completely solid at 439 degrees above

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.310
its melting point?

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:25.740
Well, the planet's gravity is so immensely
strong that it pulls the melted ice water

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:33.740
towards its core, compressing it into a solid
form, stopping it from ever evaporating, no

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:37.930
matter how much it burns.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:43.770
Next time you complain about the weather on
Earth, just stop for a moment and be thankful

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:53.440
that you don't live on the planet HD 189773b,
where it constantly rains glass, sideways.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:59.750
This planet's atmosphere is full of silicon
particles which give it it's beautiful blue

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:00.750
colour.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:06.510
But because of the planet's extremely high
surface temperatures these silicon particles

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:13.600
condense to form solid glass which flies around
the planet sideways in it's endless 4,000

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.420
mph winds.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:22.270
But hey, at least it's not as bad as living
on WASP-12b.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:28.270
This poor unfortunate planet is slowly being
eaten alive by its star.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:34.230
It's caught up in an orbit so close to its
star that the whole planet has been heated

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:40.530
up to unimaginably high temperatures and its
mass is slowly being sucked up as it hurtles

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.820
around the star extremely fast.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:49.990
The planet which is roughly the size of Jupiter,
however it appears to be larger because the

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:56.810
molten temperatures of its parent star have
caused WASP-12b to balloon up.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:04.310
This poor planet loses an incredible 6 billion
metric tonnes of mass per second.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:11.960
In fact it's being torn apart so quickly that
it's no longer a sphere, but an egg-like,

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.960
oblong shape.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.889
Next up is Gliese 581 c.

00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:23.360
This planet is very special because it's been
voted by the scientific community as one of

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.110
the top three exoplanets likely to support
alien life.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:32.230
However its very different to Earth.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:38.580
It orbits a red dwarf star so if you looked
up into the sky it would always be a deep

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.530
crimson red colour.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:46.760
The planet is also tidal locked, which means
it doesn't rotate on its axis, just like our

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:51.720
moon's relationship to Earth, one side of
the planet is always facing away from its

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.610
star and the other always facing towards it.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:06:02.610
The side of Gliese 581 c that is always facing
its red dwarf star is so blisteringly hot

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:07.419
that if you were to stand there it would melt
you alive.

00:06:07.419 --> 00:06:13.250
However the opposite side of the planet, facing
away from the star is so cold that you would

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.200
instantly freeze.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:21.370
So you may be wondering, how could this extremely
violent planet possibly support life similar

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:23.190
to humans?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:29.190
Well there is a narrow strip of land, halfway
between its hot side and its icy side that

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:32.920
is just the perfect temperature to support
life.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:39.600
But be careful not to take a step on the wrong
side or you will most certainly be toast.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:47.490
In 2008 we sent a message from Earth directly
at Gliese 581 c and it is expected to reach

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.330
the planet in 2029.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:58.060
Next up is a planet in the Scorpius constellation
known as WASP-17b.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:03.180
What makes this giant of a planet so peculiar
is its shear size.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:10.550
It is 1.9 times the size of Jupiter, which
is the largest planet in our solar system.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:15.340
It's so large that theoretically it should
not exist.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:21.810
According to scientists it breaks the laws
of how large a planet can actually get.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:26.340
For its size it also has an extremely low
density.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:33.441
Because of this it fits in to a very unique
class of planets called puffy planets, yes

00:07:33.441 --> 00:07:36.520
that's actually a scientific term.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:42.790
Puffy planets are planets with an extremely
large radius and a very low density for their

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:43.790
size.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.760
But that's not all that makes WASP-17b so
strange.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:55.240
It also has a retrograde orbit, which means
it rotates in an opposite direction to its

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.570
host star.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:05.199
You may remember that Luke Skywalker's home
planet of Tatooine in Star Wars had two suns.

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:12.100
But, as is often the case, real life can be
much more amazing than science fiction.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:19.820
149 light-years from Earth is a planet with
not one, not two, but three suns.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:27.300
This three star planet, which goes by its
catalogue name of HD 188753 Ab, sits within

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:32.090
the triple star system HD 188753.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:38.339
If you could live on this planet you would
experience triple shadows, and constant eclipses

00:08:38.339 --> 00:08:42.019
as its threes parent stars cross each other's
paths.

00:08:42.019 --> 00:08:49.230
And of course you would see the some of the
strangest and most beautiful sunsets and sunrises

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.129
in the universe.

00:08:51.129 --> 00:08:58.430
Now imagine you're in the middle of the Pacific
Ocean, the sky is blue with fluffy white clouds

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:04.490
but there's no land to be seen, in every direction
you turn is just endless water.

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:10.721
Well, that's exactly what it would be like
if you were to visit this planet 47 light

00:09:10.721 --> 00:09:18.100
years away from Earth, which goes by its catalogue
name of GJ 1214b.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:23.980
That's because its made up entirely of water,
many scientists have nicknamed this planet

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.709
the waterworld.

00:09:25.709 --> 00:09:33.079
The entire surface of the planet is one giant,
continuous ocean, and it remains the exactly

00:09:33.079 --> 00:09:39.509
the same for miles underneath the surface,
until eventually you hit the planet's core,

00:09:39.509 --> 00:09:43.110
which is made of solid ice.

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:50.749
But this isn't any ordinary ice, its not the
kind of ice you would find in your freezer.

00:09:50.749 --> 00:09:54.730
Because this ice isn't frozen due to cold
temperatures.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:59.550
The water in the planet's core is under such
immense levels of pressure from the surface

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:05.170
that the core has been compressed into solid
ice.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:11.110
This is a very special form of ice known to
scientists as ice VII (ice seven).

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.850
And last but not least.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:20.550
470 light years away is a planet discovered
by the Kepler space observatory, known as

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.279
Kepler 438b.

00:10:23.279 --> 00:10:30.399
This planet is very strange, not because it
has any extreme features, but quite the opposite.

00:10:30.399 --> 00:10:36.260
Because it is, to date, the most Earth-like
planet we have ever found.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:42.180
The Earth Similarity Index is a standard measure
of how similar to Earth another planet is.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:50.209
With a score of 1 being identical to Earth
in every way, and 0 being nothing like Earth.

00:10:50.209 --> 00:10:57.249
Kepler-438b boasts an impressive Earth Similarity
Index of 0.88.

00:10:57.249 --> 00:11:03.110
Making Kepler 438b super rare, and very special.

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:10.829
Discovered in January 2015, this planet has
all the right pre-requisites for alien life.

00:11:10.829 --> 00:11:17.790
Most importantly it is a rocky world, like
Earth and its proximity to its host star puts

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:24.139
it in what scientists call the goldilocks
zone, which is the holy grail of space exploration.

00:11:24.139 --> 00:11:29.699
The goldilocks zone is when a planet is not
too close to its parent star that it's too

00:11:29.699 --> 00:11:34.910
hot for life, yet not too far away that it's
too cold.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:41.189
Water is essential to life, where's there's
water, there's probably life, but in order

00:11:41.189 --> 00:11:48.959
to have complex life there has to be liquid
water, which most of the time can only occur

00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:51.360
in the goldilocks zone.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:12:00.759
So Kepler 438b, a rocky planet in the goldilocks
zone is highly likely to have liquid water,

00:12:00.759 --> 00:12:03.450
and therefore life.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:09.790
Which makes it one of the strangest and most
interesting exoplanets we have ever discovered.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:13.839
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

